WEBVTT

00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:04.067
Your agent has an organization of its
own and a key that can never approve.

00:00:04.067 --> 00:00:04.967
It's ready to start the setup.

00:00:04.967 --> 00:00:07.833
Answer a few questions, and
the system configures itself,

00:00:07.833 --> 00:00:10.167
with every suggestion
citing where it came from.

00:00:10.233 --> 00:00:13.933
By the end you'll know what six
screens save, what each answer changes,

00:00:13.933 --> 00:00:16.000
and which steps only a person can take.

00:00:16.067 --> 00:00:19.033
Most setup wizards collect
everything, then guess the rest.

00:00:19.033 --> 00:00:21.133
Mia gets a scoring model
that looks confident,

00:00:21.133 --> 00:00:23.100
and its numbers have no source to check.

00:00:23.133 --> 00:00:24.467
Setup works the other way.

00:00:24.467 --> 00:00:27.567
No evidence, no value: it
drafts from your own data,

00:00:27.567 --> 00:00:31.267
and a person signs what goes live.
Three rules hold on every screen.

00:00:31.267 --> 00:00:32.400
No invented values.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:35.467
Anything unknown stays empty
and becomes a numbered open ask.

00:00:35.467 --> 00:00:37.533
And the proposer never approves.

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:41.833
In the console: Setup. Or ask your
agent: "Set up GTM OS for my company".

00:00:41.833 --> 00:00:44.533
Both drive the same operations,
so you can take turns.

00:00:44.533 --> 00:00:46.367
What one saves, the other sees.

00:00:46.433 --> 00:00:49.367
Take an example. Setup suggests
a weight for company size.

00:00:49.367 --> 00:00:51.533
Beside it you see the closed
won deals it rests on,

00:00:51.533 --> 00:00:53.167
and a line from your pricing document.

00:00:53.167 --> 00:00:56.333
If a model drafted a value and cited
nothing, that value is dropped.

00:00:56.333 --> 00:00:57.533
With no model configured,

00:00:57.533 --> 00:01:00.033
a deterministic drafter fills
only what your data supports,

00:01:00.033 --> 00:01:01.200
and the card says so.

00:01:01.233 --> 00:01:04.400
Screen one is where you describe
your company: team size, markets,

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:07.633
current stack, up to three pains,
the hours a week you can spend,

00:01:07.633 --> 00:01:10.300
and your motions. The ARR
band is optional and private.

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:13.300
Only an owner or admin can read
it, and agents never see it.

00:01:13.367 --> 00:01:14.533
From your pains and motions,

00:01:14.533 --> 00:01:17.567
setup ranks the engines with
reasons and suggests blueprints.

00:01:17.567 --> 00:01:19.000
Pick yours, then click Select.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:22.033
Or ask your agent: "Which engines
and blueprint fit us, and why".

00:01:22.033 --> 00:01:24.700
Each line lists the facts
for and the facts against.

00:01:24.767 --> 00:01:28.467
Screen two, Connect your data, shows
real coverage: connected sources,

00:01:28.467 --> 00:01:32.067
records, last sync. Sources overlap,
so counts are never added up.

00:01:32.067 --> 00:01:33.033
Each source has Pull now,

00:01:33.033 --> 00:01:37.133
and every missing grant becomes a
numbered ask that names who grants it.

00:01:37.167 --> 00:01:38.433
Connecting is a human click,

00:01:38.433 --> 00:01:41.800
because OAuth consent and secret
entry stay in the console.

00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:44.267
Ask your agent: "What data
do we still need to connect".

00:01:44.267 --> 00:01:47.467
It names the gap and sends you to
Integrations, then Connections.

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:51.733
Screen three, Your definitions, starts
with your documents: PDFs with text,

00:01:51.733 --> 00:01:53.367
Word, Excel, CSV and more.

00:01:53.367 --> 00:01:55.533
Suppression lists and your data processing

00:01:55.533 --> 00:01:57.933
agreement are restricted
to owners and admins,

00:01:57.933 --> 00:01:59.167
and never go to a model.

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:02.567
Setup then drafts a card for
each of these: lifecycle stages,

00:02:02.567 --> 00:02:05.200
the ICP and its weights,
pilot scope, customer types.

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:09.333
Then who the engines never contact,
your CRM stage values, revenue truth,

00:02:09.333 --> 00:02:12.100
your words for deals, who
owns what, and brand voice.

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:13.367
Each card shows its evidence.

00:02:13.367 --> 00:02:16.633
Edit, skip, or approve, and
your edits survive a redraft.

00:02:16.633 --> 00:02:19.767
Or ask your agent: "Show me the
drafted cards and their evidence".

00:02:19.833 --> 00:02:23.500
Approving publishes through the
operation that owns that definition.

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:24.067
The ICP,

00:02:24.067 --> 00:02:27.433
scope and customer types become
proposals a different person approves.

00:02:27.433 --> 00:02:31.900
Revenue truth, deal words, territories
and brand need a signed in human,

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:33.633
because agent keys are refused.

00:02:33.667 --> 00:02:38.000
Screen four, Rules and who approves
what, holds buying roles, consent,

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:41.533
and trust settings such as Dry
Mode, caps and quiet hours.

00:02:41.533 --> 00:02:45.567
Then autonomy per engine: dry or
live, and suggest, approve each,

00:02:45.567 --> 00:02:48.833
or act within caps. Last
come seats and role profiles.

00:02:48.833 --> 00:02:51.833
The product refuses to
remove the last steward.

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:53.167
Role profiles, the ARR band,

00:02:53.167 --> 00:02:56.400
and approving cards that
target a human are human only.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:58.500
Ask your agent: "Set our role profiles".

00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:02.367
It stops and says: do this in the
console, then names the screen and button.

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:04.367
Each answer changes real behavior.

00:03:04.367 --> 00:03:07.033
The ICP card becomes the scoring
model that ranks accounts.

00:03:07.033 --> 00:03:09.267
The suppression card is
checked on every send.

00:03:09.267 --> 00:03:11.433
Consent decides which
channels reach a person,

00:03:11.433 --> 00:03:13.900
autonomy decides which
engines act without asking,

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:16.000
and territories decide who owns a lead.

00:03:16.067 --> 00:03:17.367
Screen five, The build.

00:03:17.367 --> 00:03:20.700
First, engine readiness: each
requirement is met, missing or unknown.

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:23.033
Then Run build, and a worker
job settles your cards,

00:03:23.033 --> 00:03:27.167
adapts and proposes your blueprint,
and asks about unmapped stage values.

00:03:27.167 --> 00:03:29.333
It also checks CRM completeness,
runs a dry rescore,

00:03:29.333 --> 00:03:31.533
and takes a readiness snapshot.

00:03:31.533 --> 00:03:34.567
Or ask your agent: "Start the
build and tell me what it needs".

00:03:34.600 --> 00:03:38.633
Follow the live log, retry or cancel,
and read the Needs a human list.

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:41.800
If someone changes the session
while you work, you see a conflict.

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:45.233
Re-read, then redo. Every write
names the version it was based on,

00:03:45.233 --> 00:03:47.267
so nobody overwrites anyone silently.

00:03:47.333 --> 00:03:49.900
Screen six, First motion and ninety days,

00:03:49.900 --> 00:03:52.100
gives you a plan sized
to your weekly hours.

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:55.733
Add, remove, defer or reorder plays,
or request a new one from Studio.

00:03:55.733 --> 00:03:57.967
The brief cites a brief
line for every sentence.

00:03:57.967 --> 00:04:01.667
Or ask your agent: "Show me the
ninety day plan and the brief".

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:03.767
Then Launch, which is human only.

00:04:03.767 --> 00:04:05.767
It signs and promotes
the setup definitions,

00:04:05.767 --> 00:04:08.700
and turns engines live only
where your autonomy card says so.

00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:11.700
The rest stay in Dry Mode, and a
different person approves in Approvals.

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:15.067
Ask your agent: "What does Launch
need", and it reads the preview.

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:18.133
At the end, the first win
card shows eight milestones,

00:04:18.133 --> 00:04:20.467
computed from real facts and never stored.

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:24.667
The pushback: a model drafting my
rules, then Launch switching engines on?

00:04:24.667 --> 00:04:28.367
Uncited values never survive, each
card waits on the right person,

00:04:28.367 --> 00:04:30.800
and engines go live
only where you chose it.

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:32.767
Everything else stays in Dry Mode.

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:35.600
The short version: Six
screens, every draft cited,

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:39.267
every live change signed by a
person. No evidence, no value.

00:04:39.333 --> 00:04:40.800
You answered a few questions,

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:44.900
and the system now holds evidenced
definitions, waiting on the right people.

00:04:44.900 --> 00:04:47.200
The next clip is blueprints and motions,

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:49.767
templates that seed a
whole system in one change.
